<section class="cs__sec">
  <h2 class="cs__h">What we learned</h2>
  <p class="cs__p">
    Finance leads did not need more charts. They needed to know which number was right and why.
    Trust, not visual polish, was the real brief.
  </p>
  <p class="cs__p">
    I kept the research small and specific: a handful of conversations, a look at the real data, and
    one afternoon watching people use the current product. Each finding went on a card with the
    exact words people used.
  </p>
</section>
<section class="cs__sec">
  <h2 class="cs__h">How the design came together</h2>
  <p class="cs__p">
    The dashboard starts with a single status line for the close, then lets people open any figure
    to see its sources. Charts are quiet, and exceptions are loud.
  </p>
